{#
integration/_person.html.twig — one recognised face in the people grid.

A portrait rather than a folder row: round preview, name always underneath.
"Always" is the point — a face is identified by its name, so hiding it behind
hover the way the photo grid does would make the grid unreadable. Unnamed faces
are still listed, because "who is this" is a reasonable thing to go looking for.

Navigates rather than selects: a person is a place, not something attachable.
#}
{# The mode travels with the navigation — see FilePickerController::browse(). #}
{% set navArgs = mode|default('attach') == 'avatar'
    ? { id: integration.id, folder: entry.id, mode: 'avatar' }
    : { id: integration.id, folder: entry.id, draft: draftId } %}
<a href="{{ path('app_integration_browse', navArgs) }}"
   class="group flex flex-col items-center gap-2 p-2 rounded-xl hover:bg-hover transition-colors"
   title="{{ entry.name }}">
    <span class="relative block w-24 h-24 rounded-full overflow-hidden bg-sunken ring-2 ring-transparent group-hover:ring-accent/40 transition-[box-shadow]">
        <img src="{{ path('app_integration_thumbnail', { id: integration.id, file: entry.id }) }}"
             alt="" loading="lazy" class="w-full h-full object-cover">
    </span>
    <span class="w-full truncate text-center text-xs text-ink-muted group-hover:text-ink transition-colors">
        {{ entry.name }}
    </span>
</a>
